Exactly — 4 instances × 100 = 400 connections, which blows past the postgres default of 100. 

Formula: `pool.max = floor((pg_max_connections - 10) / num_instances)`

With `max_connections=200` and 4 instances: `floor(190 / 4) = 47`, so set `max: 40` for headroom.

Also check for connection leaks — if you're not releasing clients after queries, pool exhaustion happens even at low traffic:
```javascript
// BAD — leaks if query throws
const client = await pool.connect();
const result = await client.query('SELECT ...');
client.release();

// GOOD — always releases
const result = await pool.query('SELECT ...');
```
